      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The change of the reactivity of the RAAS during physiological aging of the organism implies the variety of forms of the course of hypertension: The RAAS is involved in stage I of the development of the disease. The progress of the disease (stage III) results in the \"decay\" of the RAAS. A dependence of the activity of the RAAS on the clinical course and on the hemodynamic variant of hypertension in old age could detected."},
